        "description": "Source identity relation for the vulnerability-relevant value."
      },
      "verified": true,
      "fine_trace_step": 1,
      "description": "Source. The first byte of the PoC, `F`, matches the identifier rule and is duplicated into a heap string stored in the semantic value for token `_IDENTIFIER_`. ASan reports this allocation as a 2-byte region allocated by `__strdup` from `yara_yylex`."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "r_identifier_destructor_must_clear_c_string",
      "role": "root_cause",
      "file": "libyara/grammar.c",
      "function": "yydestruct",
      "line": 1346,
      "operands": [
        "((*yyvaluep).c_string)",
        "NULL"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "((*yyvaluep).c_string)",
        "right": "NULL"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_identifier_destructor_must_clear_c_string",
      "fine_trace_step": 4,
      "description": "Root cause. The `_IDENTIFIER_` destructor frees the token-owned string but does not clear the `YYSTYPE` slot afterwards. The dangling pointer remains in the union and is later reinterpreted as a `_REGEXP_` `sized_string` pointer. The fix changes this destructor (and the analogous token destructors) to assign the field to `NULL` immediately after `yr_free`."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_regexp_discard_second_free_sink",
      "role": "sink",
      "file": "libyara/grammar.c",
      "function": "yara_yyparse",
      "line": 3868,
      "operands": [
        "yylval->sized_string",
        "yylval.sized_string"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "yylval->sized_string",
        "right": "yylval.sized_string"
      },
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_regexp_value_reaches_discard_sink",
      "fine_trace_step": 7,
      "description": "Sink. While still in parser error recovery, `yyparse` discards the empty `_REGEXP_` lookahead. Its `%destructor` case frees `yyvaluep->sized_string`, but that union field still contains the stale identifier pointer from the first discard, so the same heap region is freed a second time. The saved ASan trace reports both the previous free and the crashing free from this `grammar.c:3868` discard path."
    },
    {
      "invariant_id": "n_regexp_token_reuses_stale_union_value",
      "verified": true,
      "verified_by": "a_stale_c_string_reaches_regexp_token",
      "role": "intermediate",
      "file": "libyara/lexer.l",
      "function": "yara_yylex",
      "line": 575,
      "fine_trace_step": 6,
      "state": "The empty-regexp return leaves `yylval->sized_string` equal to the dangling identifier pointer freed earlier, so the `_REGEXP_` token carries stale union bits instead of a fresh regexp object.",
      "operands": [
        "((*yyvaluep).c_string)",
        "yylval->sized_string"
      ],
      "relation": {
        "op": "eq",
        "left": "((*yyvaluep).c_string)",
        "right": "yylval->sized_string"
      }
    }
